1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,380
Two games from the same era use their cameras differently.

2
00:00:03,380 --> 00:00:06,040
This is the original Resident Evil2.

3
00:00:06,040 --> 00:00:09,140
The character moves, while the camera stays in its fixed position.

4
00:00:09,140 --> 00:00:11,960
The view switches to another predefined camera angle.

5
00:00:11,960 --> 00:00:16,280
Super Mario64 also lets the player choose where to look.

6
00:00:16,280 --> 00:00:17,340
In Super Mario 64,

7
00:00:17,340 --> 00:00:19,960
a character appears carrying a camera.

8
00:00:19,960 --> 00:00:23,120
Mario and the camera have separate controls.

9
00:00:23,120 --> 00:00:25,080
We will look closely, circle around,

10
00:00:25,080 --> 00:00:28,160
and pull back, in that order.

11
00:00:28,160 --> 00:00:30,400
The camera follows Mario.

12
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:33,420
The C buttons change its position and direction.

13
00:00:33,420 --> 00:00:36,040
The viewpoint is where we see the scene from.

14
00:00:36,040 --> 00:00:39,560
Turn the viewpoint to look around and upward.

15
00:00:39,560 --> 00:00:42,240
It helps you find routes and Power Stars.

16
00:00:42,240 --> 00:00:43,460
Think about where Mario stands

17
00:00:43,460 --> 00:00:46,640
separately from what the camera points toward.

18
00:00:46,640 --> 00:00:50,940
A fixed shot does not let you turn the view to inspect what is off screen.

19
00:00:50,940 --> 00:00:54,520
Mario can look in another direction while staying in the same place.

20
00:00:54,520 --> 00:00:58,360
Being able to look around before moving is the important change.

21
00:00:58,360 --> 00:01:01,000
C-up enters a close view.

22
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:03,520
The stick now looks around.

23
00:01:03,520 --> 00:01:07,120
Press A, B, or a C button other than C-up

24
00:01:07,120 --> 00:01:09,040
to return to movement control.

25
00:01:09,040 --> 00:01:11,680
Press C-left or C-right.

26
00:01:11,680 --> 00:01:13,900
The camera circles Mario.

27
00:01:13,900 --> 00:01:16,320
See the same Mario from another side.

28
00:01:16,320 --> 00:01:17,660
When the camera cannot go farther,

29
00:01:17,660 --> 00:01:19,920
a buzz signals its limit.

30
00:01:19,920 --> 00:01:21,800
Press C-down

31
00:01:21,800 --> 00:01:23,620
to pull the camera back.

32
00:01:23,620 --> 00:01:25,160
Mario looks smaller.

33
00:01:25,160 --> 00:01:27,300
More surroundings fit in view.

34
00:01:27,300 --> 00:01:29,880
Look closely, circle around, and pull back.

35
00:01:29,880 --> 00:01:31,100
In Super Mario 64,

36
00:01:31,100 --> 00:01:33,200
the player is also the cinematographer.
